---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';

// TODO(legal): this is written to be accurate rather than to be a lawyer's
// draft. Worth a review before it matters, and worth revisiting whenever a
// form, an embed or a third-party script is added to the site.
const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'hello@tomprotects.com';
const UPDATED = 'September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — TomProtects"
  description="What this site collects, where it goes, and what it does not do."
>
  <Section width="narrow">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink/60">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-ink/80">
      <p>
        This site collects one thing: your email address, and only if you choose to give it to me.
        There is no analytics, no advertising, and nothing is sold or rented to anyone.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        If you subscribe, your email address is stored in
        <a
          href="https://kit.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="font-medium text-accent underline underline-offset-4">Kit</a
        >, the service I use to send email. It is tagged with where you signed up — the home page,
        or the blog — so I can tell what people found useful. That is the whole record: an address
        and a tag.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every email has an unsubscribe link, and it works immediately. You can also ask me to delete
        your address entirely, which removes it from Kit rather than just stopping the sending.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Booking a call</h2>
      <p>
        The booking calendar on
        <a href="/workwithme" class="font-medium text-accent underline underline-offset-4"
          >Work With Me</a
        >
        is provided by TidyCal, and it is the one third-party script this site loads. The calendar
        itself runs in a frame served by TidyCal, so anything you enter to book a call — your name,
        your address, whatever you write in the notes — goes to them and is held by them, under
        <a
          href="https://tidycal.com/privacy"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="font-medium text-accent underline underline-offset-4">their privacy policy</a
        >, not this one. If you would rather not use it, email me instead and we will find a time
        that way.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">The blog</h2>
      <p>
        Posts are published to my newsletter first and pulled onto this site from Kit when you open
        a page. Reading the blog records nothing about you. Newsletters usually carry a tracking
        pixel that reports when a message is opened; those are stripped out before a post is
        rendered here, so reading a post on the web does not report anything back.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site runs on Cloudflare Pages, so requests pass through Cloudflare's network the way
        they would for any site hosted there. When you submit the signup form, your IP address is
        held briefly in memory to limit how often the form can be submitted. It is not written to
        disk, not logged, and not connected to your email address — it disappears within a minute.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">What this site does not do</h2>
      <p>
        No analytics or visitor tracking of any kind. No advertising, and no advertising trackers.
        This site sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser; the booking calendar is the
        one exception, and what it stores belongs to TidyCal rather than to me. Fonts are served
        from this site rather than from a font provider, so loading a page does not tell anyone
        else that you did. Nothing is sold, rented or shared, beyond the two services named above
        doing the jobs they are named for.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Getting in touch</h2>
      <p>
        To unsubscribe, to ask what I hold about you, or to have it deleted, email
        <a
          href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}
          class="font-medium text-accent underline underline-offset-4">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a
        >. A deletion request is done as soon as I see it, and I will confirm when it is.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
